Now I understand the vulnerability. The issue is in `InitExprToConstOffset`:

```cpp
static void InitExprToConstOffset(const InitExpr& expr, uint64_t* out_offset) {
  if (expr.insts.size() == 1) {
    switch (expr.type) {
      case InitExprType::I32:
        *out_offset = expr.insts[0].imm.i32;
        break;
      ...
```

The `expr.type` field is set in `OnI32ConstExpr`/`OnI64ConstExpr` etc., but `expr.insts` is only populated in `OnOpcode`. If the init expr contains an `i32.const` or `i64.const` opcode, `OnOpcode` pushes an `InitInst` to `insts`, and then `OnI32ConstExpr` sets `insts.back().imm.i32`. 

